 Enterprise-Grade Resume Builder Upgrade Plan                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  Context                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       The Swift Resume Builder app has solid bones (React 18, TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind, shadcn/ui, 22 templates, PDF export) but looks outdated and lacks   enterprise-grade polish and modern features. This plan upgrades the UI/UX, adds powerful new features, and introduces 10 new premium templates to     make it competitive with top resume builders like Reactive Resume and Zety.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   ---                                                                                                                                                    Phase 1: Foundation Updates (Types, State, CSS)                                                                                                       

 Files to modify:
 - src/types/resume.ts - Add new template names, add accentColor, fontFamily, sectionOrder, visibleSections fields
 - src/context/ResumeContext.tsx - Add state for accent color, font family, section ordering, section visibility, JSON import/export actions
 - src/index.css - Add new utility classes, animations, improved dark mode variables

 Changes:
 1. Extend ResumeData with optional settings object: { accentColor?: string, fontFamily?: string, sectionOrder?: string[], visibleSections?:
 Record<string, boolean> }
 2. Add 10 new template names to TemplateName union
 3. Add context methods: updateSettings, exportToJson, importFromJson, reorderSections, toggleSectionVisibility
 4. Add CSS keyframe animations: fadeIn, slideUp, scaleIn
 5. Add glassmorphism utility classes

 ---
 Phase 2: UI/UX Modernization

 Files to modify:
 - src/components/Navbar.tsx - Add dark mode toggle, improved branding, glass-effect navbar
 - src/pages/Index.tsx - Redesign with hero header, progress bar, better layout
 - src/components/ResumeForm.tsx - Add section visibility toggles, drag-and-drop handles, JSON import/export buttons, font/color pickers, ATS score    
 display, completion progress
 - src/components/ResumePreview.tsx - Pass accent color and font family to templates, add print button
 - src/components/TemplateSelector.tsx - Larger thumbnails, hover effects, template count badges per category, "NEW" badge on new templates
 - src/components/Footer.tsx - Update template count stat
 - src/components/InfoSection.tsx - Add ATS score explanation

 Key changes:
 1. Navbar: Add sun/moon dark mode toggle using next-themes (already in dependencies), modernize with glass effect
 2. Index page: Add a polished header with gradient text, completion progress bar, better section titles
 3. ResumeForm:
   - Add "Customize" section at top with accent color picker (8 preset colors) and font family selector (6 fonts)
   - Add JSON Export/Import buttons in the controls area
   - Add eye icons on each accordion section to toggle visibility
   - Add ATS score badge showing a score 0-100
   - Add drag handles (grip icon) on experience/education/project cards
 4. ResumePreview: Pass settings to templates, add a Print button
 5. TemplateSelector: Bigger preview cards, "NEW" badges, better grid

 ---
 Phase 3: New Features Implementation

 3a. JSON Import/Export

 - Export: Serialize ResumeData to JSON file, trigger download
 - Import: File input that reads JSON, validates schema with basic checks, loads into state
 - Add buttons in ResumeForm controls area

 3b. Accent Color Customization

 - 8 preset colors: Blue, Teal, Purple, Rose, Amber, Emerald, Slate, Red
 - Color picker UI in form's "Customize" section
 - Templates receive accentColor and apply it to their accent elements
 - Store in settings, persist with localStorage

 3c. Font Family Picker

 - 6 options: Inter, Georgia, Merriweather, Roboto, Playfair Display, Source Sans Pro
 - Dropdown in "Customize" section
 - Templates apply the font to their body text

 3d. Section Visibility Toggles

 - Eye/eye-off icon button on each accordion section header
 - Hidden sections don't render in preview
 - Stored in settings

 3e. ATS Score Checker

 - Simple rule-based scoring (no AI needed):
   - Has name (+10), has email (+10), has phone (+5), has summary (+10), summary length 150-300 chars (+5)
   - Has at least 1 experience (+10), experience has bullet points (+5)
   - Has education (+5), has skills (+10), 5-15 skills (+5)
   - Has measurable metrics in bullets (numbers/percentages) (+10)
   - Total up to 100
 - Display as a badge/meter in the form header area

 3f. Print Support

 - Add Print button next to Download PDF
 - Use window.print() with a print-specific CSS media query

 ---
 Phase 4: 10 New Premium Templates

 New files to create (each in src/components/templates/):

 1. SwissTemplate.tsx - Ultra-clean grid, Helvetica/Inter, Swiss design. Red accent line, geometric precision
 2. MetroTemplate.tsx - Flat design, bold tile-like sections, strong typography hierarchy
 3. LuxeTemplate.tsx - Dark navy/gold, serif fonts, high-end luxury brand feel
 4. NordicTemplate.tsx - Soft pastels (light blue/cream), airy spacing, gentle rounded elements
 5. ArchitectTemplate.tsx - Blueprint aesthetic, technical grid lines, monospace details
 6. EditorialTemplate.tsx - Newspaper column layout, drop caps, elegant serif typography
 7. BrutalistTemplate.tsx - Thick black borders, raw typography, asymmetric layout, trendy
 8. GlassTemplate.tsx - Soft gradients, frosted glass card sections, modern glassmorphism
 9. NeonTemplate.tsx - Dark background, neon cyan/magenta accents, cyberpunk aesthetic
 10. PixelTemplate.tsx - Retro pixel-art vibe, monospace font, dot-matrix borders, fun

 For each template:
 - Create as standalone file (not in AllTemplates.tsx)
 - Follow existing pattern: export default function XTemplate({ data }: { data: ResumeData })
 - Support accent color override from settings
 - Support font family override from settings
 - Inline styles at 794x1123px canvas
 - Add lazy loader in ResumePreview.tsx
 - Add to TemplateSelector.tsx with thumbnail
 - Add PDF color config in ResumePreview.tsx

 After templates: Update TemplateName type, update all lookup maps

 ---
 Phase 5: Integration & Polish

 1. Update src/components/pdf/PdfTemplates.tsx - Add PDF color configs for all 10 new templates
 2. Update src/components/Footer.tsx - Change "22+" to "32+" templates
 3. Test all templates with example data and empty data
 4. Verify PDF export works for all templates
 5. Test dark mode across all pages
 6. Test mobile responsiveness
 7. Verify localStorage persistence includes new settings

 ---
 Implementation Order

 1. Phase 1 (types + state + CSS) ~10 min
 2. Phase 4 (new templates - most impactful, visible change) ~40 min
 3. Phase 2 (UI modernization) ~25 min
 4. Phase 3 (new features) ~25 min
 5. Phase 5 (integration + polish) ~10 min

